  "rules": [
    "A citation without a recognized URL keeps its existing template family and access-date metadata. No publication kind is inferred from a publisher, domain or missing field.",
    "Existing native Citation calls remain generic bibliographic references. Citação and Citar are text-quotation templates, not bibliographic aliases.",
    "Only source profiles whose pinned implementation declares a reviewed news class receive Citar jornal. The existing finite parameter map is retained and every mapped key must be accepted by the native target.",
    "Unsupported fields and conflicting values block the foreign-template migration rather than being discarded. Native template aliases remain governed by the existing valid-alias preservation rule.",
    "The preservation audit and diff-composition guard bind the declared citation family, or its approved foreign migration, to the same title, URL, DOI, ISBN, PMID and PMC anchors and access-date values. Recognized bibliographic templates outside ref tags receive the same check.",
    "Retention compares sets of those semantic obligations, allowing identical references to share a definition without requiring duplicate citation bodies. This guard supplements the existing reference and content checks; it is not a proof of every bibliographic field.",
    "A migration refused only because a formerly accepted generic CS1 key is unsupported by the reviewed native newspaper template keeps the original source quietly. This bounded refusal adds no migration warning, foreign-template alert or partial-conversion proposal. Existing unknown-field and conflicting-value warnings remain."
  ]
